\section*{Hodge classes on generic abelian-cover Jacobian powers}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For tensor-Hodge-generic abelian-cover Jacobians and the specified very general diagonal complete intersections, OpenAI claims the rational Hodge assertion on every self-power. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 032, 2026-09-30): Deck-character projections and equivariant period calculations identify the necessary monodromy invariants of curve covers. Correspondences dominated by CM sources supply determinant tensors, while Gale duality transfers the character-level construction to diagonal complete intersections with the required supports and degree shifts.

